  "interpretation_guide": [
    "attainable_fraction is the share of the baseline-to-noise-floor gap a model closed; 0 means no better than the best non-learned baseline, 1 means it reached the floor.",
    "A model that only recognises mechanism classes should score well on the reference arm and near 0 on leave-one-class-out, especially for the HDAC fold.",
    "A stratum whose baseline already sits at its replicate floor has no attainable signal, so a fraction near 0 there is expected rather than a model failure."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Classes come from sci-Plex/ChEMBL annotations, not from the expression data, but they are coarse and some compounds are polypharmacological.",
    "Leave-one-class-out changes the training set size between folds.",
    "Strata are computed on the test groups of each reference split, so stratum sizes vary by seed."
  ]
